memtest86 (1.1.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * GUI polish iteration
    - Fix title bar icon: use the app's memtest86 icon (was "diagnostics")
    - Test checkboxes in a 3-column grid + Select-all / Clear-all links;
      configuration group is compact and no longer squeezes the status area
    - Show system memory total/available to help pick a test size
    - Start/Stop dual buttons (DSuggestButton / DWarningButton), swapped by
      state, with immediate style feedback
    - Release the test buffer on stop/finish so memory returns to the system
    - All long test loops now poll the stop flag every 2 MiB: stop responds
      within milliseconds even on multi-GiB buffers (was seconds)
    - finished() reports bytes actually tested when stopped mid-run
      (previously 0 on early stop)
    - i18n: new GUI strings translated (zh_CN)

 -- lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>  Tue, 18 Aug 2025 20:20:00 +0800

memtest86 (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Iteration: core algorithm and robustness improvements
    - Test 4/7 (random patterns) now replay the PRNG sequence from a fixed
      seed instead of storing an expected[] vector: peak memory halved
    - Test 4 invert pass uses read-modify-write from the tail (memtest86
      moving-inversions semantics), so fill-phase corruption is detected
    - Test 9 bit fade: real configurable idle delay (--fade-delay, default
      1000 ms) between write and verify
    - Buffer allocation: best-effort mlock + MADV_HUGEPAGE (never fatal)
    - New --self-test mode: injects a known single-bit fault and verifies
      the detection logic reports it; also checks a clean buffer yields no
      false positives
    - Test 6 (32-bit blocks) now uses the same checkDWord helper as the
      other tests for consistent error recording
    - translationDir() prefers a tree-local translations/ dir so rebuilt
      .qm files win over an older installed copy (dev workflow)
    - i18n: new help/self-test strings translated (zh_CN)

 -- lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>  Mon, 18 Aug 2025 13:30:00 +0800

memtest86 (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release for deepin 25.
  * Memory diagnostic tool inspired by memtest86:
    - 9 test algorithms (walking ones, own address, moving inversions,
      block move, random sequence, bit fade)
    - CLI mode and DTK6 GUI mode
    - i18n following system locale (Chinese / English)
    - App icon, desktop entry, man page, debian packaging

